Important discovery: `ChatGptOAuthLocalCallbackServer.callbackUrl` says:

```
// Mirror the original codex-rs redirect URI exactly
// (server.rs: `format!("http://localhost:{port}/auth/callback")`)
// — auth.openai.com rejects 127.0.0.1 as an off-list host.
: 'http://localhost:${server.port}/auth/callback';
```

So auth.openai.com REJECTS `127.0.0.1` as an off-list host — only `localhost` is registered. The new iOS flow uses `http://localhost:1455/auth/callback` — consistent with the registered host. Good. And the canonical port 1455 keeps it predictable. Good.

But — the macOS server binds port 1455 or 1457 with fallback. On iOS no port is bound so no conflict. Good.

Now, one thing to check: does the webview navigation decision accept `127.0.0.1` — yes it does (both hosts). Since auth.openai.com redirects only to localhost (per its registration), 127.0.0.1 acceptance is harmless. But hmm — the redirect happens via HTTP 302 from the server; the server will redirect to `http://localhost:1455/auth/callback?...`. The delegate prevents it. Good.

