💡 **SUGGESTION: near-total structural duplication with `CodeMieSsoWebViewPage`**

The PR deliberately mirrors the CodeMie page, but the overlap is now ~120 lines of byte-similar code across the two files: the `_loading`/`_errorMessage`/`_timeoutTimer`/`_completed` state block, `_createController()` plumbing (JS mode, delegate wiring, `loadRequest`), `onWebResourceError` main-frame filtering, `_onTimeout`/pop-with-null, the `faAppBar` + progress indicator, and the identical error-banner `Stack`/`Positioned`/`Material` subtree in `build()`.

A shared scaffold would collapse most of it, e.g. a generic

```dart
class OAuthWebViewScaffold extends StatefulWidget {
  const OAuthWebViewScaffold({
    required this.initialUrl,
    required this.onNavigationRequest, // per-flow decision (token vs code)
    this.onPageFinished,               // per-flow body sniff
    this.title, this.timeout = const Duration(minutes: 5),
  });
}
```

with the per-flow differences (the `NavigationDecision` predicate and the Google-block sniff) injected — both decision helpers are already pure top-level functions, so they slot straight in. That extraction would also let the "clear the banner on navigation start" fix (see the other thread) land once for both flows. Fine as a follow-up; not a merge blocker since the ticket scoped this page as a CodeMie mirror.

